CAVEAT:  The title names two modes, "promiscuous" and "intercept".  This build has no command to choose a
         mode.  Interception is on without any configuration.  The AW+ Technical Tips and Tricks guide
         (p.73, p.78) describes the older modes.  In "promiscuous" mode the switch also acts as the
         client's gateway.  This run did not test that part.  The port has `auth forward arp`, so the DUT
         forwards the client's ARP.  HTTPS (TCP 443) interception was not tested.  Only one destination
         address, 8.8.8.8, was used.
