  => STEP 4 PASS: after the login, the same SYNs went to the DUT's MAC.  The DUT did not answer
     them as 8.8.8.8.  It sent 2 ICMP type 3 code 0 (network unreachable) from 192.168.50.1.  The
     host reports this ICMP as Errno 101.  So the DUT routed the traffic, and it has no route to
     8.8.8.8.  The intercept stops for a client that has logged in, even with `intercept-port any`.
